# Docker build context is the repo root (render.yaml dockerContext: .).
# Keep secrets out, keep the context small, and never ship a stale build artifact.

# --- secrets ---
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.pem
**/*.pem
# Exception: the client's VITE_* values are not secrets — they are compiled
# into the public JS bundle by Vite, so excluding them buys nothing and breaks
# the build. client/.env.production is the only env file Vite reads during
# `npm run build` in the Dockerfile (mode=production), and VITE_PRIVY_APP_ID
# has NO code fallback: without it PrivyProvider renders children unauthenticated
# and every Privy feature is disabled in production, no matter what is set in
# Render. Keep server/.env and server/.env.production excluded above this line.
!client/.env.production

# --- repo hygiene ---
.git
.github
**/node_modules
# Must stay excluded. server/dist was tracked in git before .gitignore covered
# it, and git keeps tracking files it already tracks — so it sat in the repo
# long after the ignore rule existed. The Dockerfile compiles fresh, but a
# committed or local dist/ inside the build context merges into the image's own
# output: files deleted from src/ survive as stale JS. The image would build,
# pass its health check, and serve code that no longer exists in source.
**/dist
**/build
**/.next
**/.cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/logs
**/uploads
**/*.log

# --- credentials and media that must never reach an image ---
*.csv
*.mp4
*.zip
*.deb
*.pptx
*.pdf
brag-output-*
foundation-sites/
OpenWA/
Pabandi_ui/
strix/
globe-gen/
promo-video/
videos/
video-ads/
marketing-bot/
OpenMontage/
.idea/
.vscode/
